1
00:00:31,865 --> 00:00:37,500
<i>On the 12th, a fire broke out at Changnyeong
Myeongin's soy sauce factory in Andong.</i>

2
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:40,304
<i>Company president Cho Yeong Gwang
was found at the scene.</i>

3
00:00:40,304 --> 00:00:44,083
<i>He was taken to the hospital but later died.</i>

4
00:00:44,083 --> 00:00:47,988
<i>Fire officials believe
it started from an overheated machine...</i>

5
00:00:50,926 --> 00:00:52,829
<i>Hello.</i>

6
00:01:25,419 --> 00:01:29,019
[10. The Summer We Grew Up]

7
00:02:25,202 --> 00:02:26,229
[Episode 10]

8
00:02:26,229 --> 00:02:28,428
Aren't you guys hot?

9
00:02:31,401 --> 00:02:33,106
- Cha Tae Su.
- Here.

10
00:02:33,106 --> 00:02:34,564
- Choi Go Un.
- Here.

11
00:02:34,564 --> 00:02:36,057
- Choi Jang Hee.
- Here.

12
00:02:36,057 --> 00:02:37,875
- Choi Jeong Ho.
- Here.

13
00:02:37,875 --> 00:02:39,428
- Pyo Su Yeon.
- Here.

14
00:02:39,428 --> 00:02:40,849
- Heo Yi Hyeon.
- Here.

15
00:02:40,849 --> 00:02:43,098
- Kim Ha Yeon.
- Here.

16
00:02:52,638 --> 00:02:55,594
Is it true Cho Yu Gyeom's grandpa died?

17
00:03:01,598 --> 00:03:03,741
Sir, here's the thing.

18
00:03:03,741 --> 00:03:06,182
Cho Yu Gyeom's grandpa passed away, right?

19
00:03:06,182 --> 00:03:07,822
I know.

20
00:03:07,822 --> 00:03:10,148
It was even on the news.

21
00:03:10,148 --> 00:03:13,851
So Cho Yu Gyeom can't compete, right?

22
00:03:15,650 --> 00:03:17,464
What are you hoping for?

23
00:03:17,464 --> 00:03:22,411
Honestly, I'm torn right down the middle.

24
00:03:22,411 --> 00:03:26,456
It's so sad that Cho Yu Gyeom's grandpa died.

25
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:31,376
But part of me hopes he'll sit out
the competition because of it.

26
00:03:32,754 --> 00:03:34,555
What does that make me?

27
00:03:35,347 --> 00:03:38,399
Well, is that a cowardly thing to feel?

28
00:03:38,399 --> 00:03:39,773
Come on!

29
00:03:39,773 --> 00:03:41,289
It's okay.

30
00:03:42,204 --> 00:03:45,266
I didn't feel the least bit sad.

31
00:03:45,266 --> 00:03:49,272
I just checked if the final could be postponed
due to a grandparent's death.

32
00:03:50,971 --> 00:03:53,385
What's that supposed to mean?

33
00:03:56,749 --> 00:03:59,156
- Let's practice.
- Again?

34
00:03:59,156 --> 00:04:00,899
Come on, we're out of time.

35
00:04:00,899 --> 00:04:02,868
- Seriously.
- Come on.

36
00:04:02,868 --> 00:04:04,682
Let's go!

37
00:04:09,315 --> 00:04:10,669
Yu Gyeom.

38
00:04:15,774 --> 00:04:18,663
Yu Gyeom, come eat something.

39
00:04:19,811 --> 00:04:21,203
No.

40
00:04:21,872 --> 00:04:24,486
You haven't eaten a single meal.

41
00:04:26,099 --> 00:04:28,125
I said no.

42
00:04:48,816 --> 00:04:51,937
[Changnyeong Myeongin fire]

43
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:08,813
Would you accept my apology?

44
00:05:14,501 --> 00:05:15,878
Thank you.

45
00:05:28,550 --> 00:05:31,190
Didn't you laugh at what I said back then?

46
00:05:31,190 --> 00:05:32,860
Sure I did.

47
00:05:33,566 --> 00:05:35,523
It was so funny.

48
00:05:36,681 --> 00:05:40,606
But then I apologized to Kim Jin Mi once.

49
00:05:41,925 --> 00:05:47,677
Back then, I just blurted it out
because she scared me.

50
00:05:48,473 --> 00:05:50,028
But...

51
00:05:51,095 --> 00:05:52,773
She cried.

52
00:05:53,566 --> 00:05:54,920
And you?

53
00:05:55,898 --> 00:05:57,789
I felt sad too.

54
00:06:01,554 --> 00:06:03,693
But it's harder than I thought.

55
00:06:04,312 --> 00:06:07,259
You said all I had to do was apologize.

56
00:06:07,259 --> 00:06:10,996
Jin Mi and Na Gyeong were pretty understanding.

57
00:06:10,996 --> 00:06:14,750
But some kids got even angrier than I did.

58
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:16,126
And...

59
00:06:16,126 --> 00:06:21,222
Some even told me to take
as many hits as I gave them.

60
00:06:22,632 --> 00:06:26,688
And some said they still couldn't forgive me.

61
00:06:27,315 --> 00:06:29,935
What did you say to them?

62
00:06:32,484 --> 00:06:34,267
That...

63
00:06:35,467 --> 00:06:37,429
That I was sorry anyway.

64
00:06:40,442 --> 00:06:41,669
Good.

65
00:06:42,679 --> 00:06:44,350
You did the right thing.

66
00:06:49,399 --> 00:06:54,641
But I always thought apologizing
was for the other person.

67
00:06:55,379 --> 00:06:56,590
Yes.

68
00:06:57,982 --> 00:06:59,401
It wasn't.

69
00:07:01,190 --> 00:07:03,323
It wasn't?

70
00:07:03,323 --> 00:07:05,924
No, it wasn't.

71
00:07:06,927 --> 00:07:08,721
It's so weird.

72
00:07:08,721 --> 00:07:11,280
When I apologize, I feel at peace.

73
00:07:12,276 --> 00:07:14,371
Yes, that's right.

74
00:07:14,371 --> 00:07:17,002
It's something I do for myself.

75
00:07:20,565 --> 00:07:21,658
Right.

76
00:07:28,282 --> 00:07:30,771
Okay. Then I'm sorry too, Sung Sae Ryeong.

77
00:07:31,607 --> 00:07:32,858
What?

78
00:07:32,858 --> 00:07:36,316
You said I hurt you too.

79
00:07:38,512 --> 00:07:41,618
I never meant to take
Cho Yu Gyeom away from you.

80
00:07:44,422 --> 00:07:47,755
I used to say that a lot.

81
00:07:47,755 --> 00:07:49,678
I never meant to hurt you.

82
00:07:49,678 --> 00:07:51,114
Things like that.

83
00:07:55,737 --> 00:07:57,545
And thank you.

84
00:07:58,943 --> 00:08:00,559
You're thanking me?

85
00:08:02,088 --> 00:08:03,638
Yes.

86
00:08:03,638 --> 00:08:05,402
The truth is...

87
00:08:05,402 --> 00:08:09,549
I'm always the one who gets picked on
by people like you.

88
00:08:09,549 --> 00:08:15,344
So what you're doing now is a comfort to me.

89
00:08:16,023 --> 00:08:18,457
It's not like I apologized to you.

90
00:08:18,457 --> 00:08:20,818
So why is it comforting?

91
00:08:24,630 --> 00:08:27,370
It makes me see that what I went through...

92
00:08:29,009 --> 00:08:32,236
It wasn't my fault.

93
00:08:57,042 --> 00:08:58,489
Yu Gyeom?

94
00:09:00,855 --> 00:09:02,958
Yu Gyeom, come eat.

95
00:09:05,045 --> 00:09:07,365
You're really not eating anything?

96
00:09:09,149 --> 00:09:10,526
Cho Yu Gyeom.

97
00:09:11,357 --> 00:09:12,781
Don't touch me.

98
00:09:15,634 --> 00:09:17,411
You're not even my mom.

99
00:09:18,037 --> 00:09:19,299
Get out.

100
00:09:22,329 --> 00:09:23,704
No.

101
00:09:24,551 --> 00:09:26,398
I am your mother.

102
00:09:31,824 --> 00:09:33,182
No, you're not.

103
00:09:40,872 --> 00:09:46,866
I have never once neglected you
or taken you for granted.

104
00:09:46,866 --> 00:09:50,149
I always devoted myself to you...

105
00:09:50,149 --> 00:09:51,524
But you never liked me.

106
00:09:51,524 --> 00:09:54,101
- What?
- You were just forcing it.

107
00:09:56,691 --> 00:09:58,765
That's why you ran to your daughter first.

108
00:09:58,765 --> 00:10:00,309
Yu Gyeom, that's...

109
00:10:00,309 --> 00:10:01,808
Because...

110
00:10:02,732 --> 00:10:05,387
She's your own child, and I'm--

111
00:10:05,387 --> 00:10:06,841
Hey!

112
00:10:12,696 --> 00:10:13,985
What?

113
00:10:23,107 --> 00:10:24,566
Did you just yell at me?

114
00:10:24,566 --> 00:10:25,792
Yes, I did.

115
00:10:25,792 --> 00:10:28,885
How did you keep from yelling at me until now?

116
00:10:29,505 --> 00:10:33,961
How did you keep from getting angry at me
and hating me all this time?

117
00:10:33,961 --> 00:10:35,749
I didn't hold back!

118
00:10:37,387 --> 00:10:39,304
I never felt that way!

119
00:10:39,304 --> 00:10:41,022
Me too!

120
00:10:42,663 --> 00:10:44,073
I...

121
00:10:45,521 --> 00:10:48,482
I know you're not my mom.

122
00:10:48,482 --> 00:10:51,783
I know my aunt is the one who gave birth to me!

123
00:10:53,279 --> 00:10:55,972
But I didn't want to believe it.

124
00:10:55,972 --> 00:10:59,899
Just the fact that she gave birth to me
felt like a nightmare.

125
00:10:59,899 --> 00:11:05,767
So I kept believing you were my real
mom, even when people said I was adopted!

126
00:11:08,460 --> 00:11:09,743
No.

127
00:11:12,315 --> 00:11:14,431
You are my real mom.

128
00:11:17,281 --> 00:11:19,790
- Yu Gyeom.
- But, seriously.

129
00:11:20,832 --> 00:11:23,120
The really stupid thing is...

130
00:11:25,182 --> 00:11:27,872
no matter how much I tell myself,

131
00:11:29,472 --> 00:11:31,865
it was never going to make you...

132
00:11:34,528 --> 00:11:36,399
my real mom.

133
00:11:45,622 --> 00:11:47,315
<i>Father.</i>

134
00:11:47,315 --> 00:11:50,127
<i>Who said you could call me Father?</i>

135
00:11:50,127 --> 00:11:51,587
<i>Sir.</i>

136
00:11:51,587 --> 00:11:52,962
<i>Give me Yu Gyeom now.</i>

137
00:11:52,962 --> 00:11:55,833
<i>Please. You have raised him long enough.</i>

138
00:11:55,833 --> 00:11:57,467
<i>He's not an object.</i>

139
00:11:57,467 --> 00:12:00,079
<i>But you took him from me.</i>

140
00:12:01,346 --> 00:12:05,016
<i>Father, I gave birth to Yu Gyeom.</i>

141
00:12:05,016 --> 00:12:08,138
<i>So let me take him now. Please?</i>

142
00:12:08,138 --> 00:12:10,813
<i>You've forgotten what you traded Yu Gyeom for.</i>

143
00:12:10,813 --> 00:12:12,733
<i>I can give it back to you.</i>

144
00:12:12,733 --> 00:12:15,569
<i>You're the one who gave him up.</i>

145
00:12:15,569 --> 00:12:20,324
<i>Yu Gyeom and I, for money and a house...</i>

146
00:12:20,324 --> 00:12:22,171
<i>Yu Gyeom!</i>

147
00:12:23,478 --> 00:12:25,523
<i>My girl!</i>

148
00:12:25,523 --> 00:12:27,456
<i>Grandpa!</i>

149
00:12:27,456 --> 00:12:31,208
<i>My girl! Oh my, my sweet girl.</i>

150
00:12:34,065 --> 00:12:35,317
<i>Go.</i>

151
00:12:45,816 --> 00:12:48,108
<i>What on earth is wrong with him?</i>

152
00:12:48,108 --> 00:12:50,774
<i>Even the hospital doesn't know.</i>

153
00:12:50,774 --> 00:12:52,829
<i>This is driving me crazy.</i>

154
00:13:12,504 --> 00:13:13,997
<i>Yu Gyeom.</i>

155
00:13:58,338 --> 00:13:59,949
Are you okay?

156
00:14:03,669 --> 00:14:05,496
Are you really okay?

157
00:14:12,357 --> 00:14:13,977
Grandpa...

158
00:14:16,399 --> 00:14:18,687
I mean, Grandpa...

159
00:14:18,687 --> 00:14:23,236
<i>If you try to get what you want,
you lose something precious.</i>

160
00:14:24,107 --> 00:14:26,365
<i>Yu Gyeom, what will you lose?</i>

161
00:14:26,365 --> 00:14:28,005
<i>You, Grandfather.</i>

162
00:14:28,660 --> 00:14:30,051
<i>What?</i>

163
00:14:31,205 --> 00:14:32,693
I...

164
00:14:34,041 --> 00:14:36,013
I feel so bad.

165
00:14:37,940 --> 00:14:39,644
To Grandpa...

166
00:14:41,149 --> 00:14:42,992
I said something like that.

167
00:14:45,149 --> 00:14:47,439
And I never even apologized.

168
00:14:51,850 --> 00:14:53,978
I couldn't do anything for him.

169
00:15:00,107 --> 00:15:01,989
And now even Mom...

170
00:15:12,162 --> 00:15:13,653
Mom...

171
00:15:15,596 --> 00:15:17,379
Grandpa...

172
00:15:19,859 --> 00:15:21,211
Mom...

173
00:15:23,673 --> 00:15:25,320
Jeez!

174
00:15:26,968 --> 00:15:29,887
You psycho, why the hell are you crying?

175
00:15:29,887 --> 00:15:31,678
Are you the only one who's sad?

176
00:15:31,678 --> 00:15:34,758
Seriously, I told you not to hit me!

177
00:15:34,758 --> 00:15:35,936
That's correct.

178
00:15:35,936 --> 00:15:37,563
Why do you keep hitting him?

179
00:15:37,563 --> 00:15:39,766
There's nowhere left to hit.

180
00:15:44,777 --> 00:15:45,846
No.

181
00:15:45,846 --> 00:15:48,365
Stop it, I said!

182
00:15:48,365 --> 00:15:50,492
What?

183
00:15:50,492 --> 00:15:52,369
What is it?

184
00:15:52,369 --> 00:15:54,325
What do you mean she's not your mom?

185
00:15:55,997 --> 00:15:57,508
No. Over something that small?

186
00:15:59,333 --> 00:16:03,630
So what if she came to save me?

187
00:16:03,630 --> 00:16:08,760
Your mom raised a foundling like you
for 18 years!

188
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:11,206
That can happen!

189
00:16:12,149 --> 00:16:14,524
It's how she truly feels.

190
00:16:14,524 --> 00:16:17,107
In the end, that's why she saved you, not me.

191
00:16:17,107 --> 00:16:18,443
Isn't it?

192
00:16:19,649 --> 00:16:21,480
No.

193
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:22,596
Hey.

194
00:16:22,596 --> 00:16:27,200
How can that split-second decision
show how she really feels?

195
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:30,156
For 18 years, you weren't even her own kid.

196
00:16:30,156 --> 00:16:33,659
But she treasured you like gold.

197
00:16:33,659 --> 00:16:39,648
That's how she really feels!

198
00:16:39,648 --> 00:16:41,210
No.

199
00:16:41,210 --> 00:16:42,945
No. That's how she really feels.

200
00:16:51,876 --> 00:16:56,899
Whatever. Quit your crying and get inside.

201
00:16:56,899 --> 00:17:01,188
Even someone like you is the head-family heir,
so the guests are all asking for you.

202
00:17:01,188 --> 00:17:02,617
You should go!

203
00:17:44,314 --> 00:17:45,791
Sister.

204
00:17:51,365 --> 00:17:53,101
Thank you.

205
00:17:57,665 --> 00:17:59,021
Forget it.

206
00:18:07,379 --> 00:18:08,975
<i>Let's break up.</i>

207
00:18:10,048 --> 00:18:11,089
<i>What?</i>

208
00:18:15,469 --> 00:18:16,607
<i>Break up?</i>

209
00:18:16,607 --> 00:18:18,504
<i>Yes, it's come to that.</i>

210
00:18:22,418 --> 00:18:24,441
<i>- Why?
- I'm getting married.</i>

211
00:18:28,042 --> 00:18:34,030
<i>You're really going to marry some woman
your family picked for you?</i>

212
00:18:34,030 --> 00:18:36,241
<i>Yes, I have to.</i>

213
00:18:36,241 --> 00:18:38,235
<i>You must be out of your mind.</i>

214
00:18:40,271 --> 00:18:41,662
<i>Hey.</i>

215
00:18:41,662 --> 00:18:42,976
<i>Then...</i>

216
00:18:43,995 --> 00:18:46,130
<i>Get married, then come back.</i>

217
00:18:46,130 --> 00:18:48,022
<i>I'll wait for you.</i>

218
00:18:48,022 --> 00:18:49,045
<i>No.</i>

219
00:18:49,045 --> 00:18:51,827
<i>Divorce isn't an option in my family.</i>

220
00:18:54,777 --> 00:18:56,278
<i>Cho Jae Jin.</i>

221
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:59,262
<i>Do you ever do anything you want?</i>

222
00:18:59,262 --> 00:19:00,274
<i>No.</i>

223
00:19:00,274 --> 00:19:02,183
<i>I just live the way I'm told. So...</i>

224
00:19:02,183 --> 00:19:04,320
<i>Come back, you lunatic.</i>

225
00:19:04,320 --> 00:19:06,319
<i>After you get married.</i>

226
00:19:13,521 --> 00:19:15,047
<i>Jae Jin!</i>

227
00:19:21,453 --> 00:19:23,125
<i>You came back.</i>

228
00:19:36,176 --> 00:19:37,734
That night.

229
00:19:38,940 --> 00:19:41,204
Why did I go to you?

230
00:19:42,473 --> 00:19:48,739
So are you saying that us having
Yu Gyeom was the wrong choice?

231
00:19:48,739 --> 00:19:50,604
No.

232
00:19:50,604 --> 00:19:54,940
I'm saying the result was a blessing,
but the process was terrible.

233
00:19:54,940 --> 00:19:57,919
And that's entirely my fault.

234
00:19:59,741 --> 00:20:02,033
Yes, it's my fault.

235
00:20:02,666 --> 00:20:06,482
A man with a wife and child
went to see his old girlfriend.

236
00:20:06,482 --> 00:20:08,374
Still, I'm his mother.

237
00:20:08,374 --> 00:20:10,755
Yes. You're Cho Yu Gyeom's mother.

238
00:20:11,816 --> 00:20:15,247
So I'll set up a time for you two to meet.

239
00:20:15,247 --> 00:20:19,107
I'll somehow convince Yu Gyeom to see you
once a week or every other week.

240
00:20:19,107 --> 00:20:21,524
Then you can see him as often as you like.

241
00:20:21,524 --> 00:20:24,247
Cho Jae Jin, please don't do this to me.

242
00:20:24,247 --> 00:20:25,517
It was always me.

243
00:20:25,517 --> 00:20:27,472
You always chose me.

244
00:20:27,472 --> 00:20:29,221
Did you forget, Jae Jin?

245
00:20:30,223 --> 00:20:31,709
That's why...

246
00:20:32,440 --> 00:20:34,988
That's why I always felt guilty about Ji Yeong.

247
00:20:35,615 --> 00:20:37,741
Whatever I did, I couldn't be forgiven.

248
00:20:37,741 --> 00:20:40,741
Because of the wrong choice I made back then.

249
00:20:40,741 --> 00:20:42,940
Don't just take it from me.

250
00:20:42,940 --> 00:20:46,919
Your wife had better beat you up too. Got it?

251
00:21:02,179 --> 00:21:04,415
You're going, right?

252
00:21:07,810 --> 00:21:09,016
Yes.

253
00:21:11,607 --> 00:21:12,887
Okay.

254
00:21:18,036 --> 00:21:20,675
You won't be at school tomorrow, right?

255
00:21:21,691 --> 00:21:22,864
Right.

256
00:21:28,705 --> 00:21:30,377
The day after tomorrow too?

257
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:32,807
Yes.

258
00:21:37,225 --> 00:21:38,858
Okay.

259
00:21:38,858 --> 00:21:41,424
Then what about that evening?

260
00:21:43,053 --> 00:21:44,902
I'll come pick you up.

261
00:21:46,399 --> 00:21:47,930
What?

262
00:21:47,930 --> 00:21:49,488
That evening.

263
00:21:51,228 --> 00:21:52,549
How's that?

264
00:22:16,858 --> 00:22:19,732
<i>Sam Hee, my dear.</i>

265
00:22:19,732 --> 00:22:22,190
<i>Yes, Grandpa.</i>

266
00:22:22,190 --> 00:22:23,899
<i>Now, now.</i>

267
00:22:23,899 --> 00:22:27,262
<i>These flowers are so pretty.</i>

268
00:22:27,262 --> 00:22:29,508
<i>Yes, they're really pretty.</i>

269
00:22:29,508 --> 00:22:31,774
<i>They're just like you, Sam Hee.</i>

270
00:22:31,774 --> 00:22:33,295
<i>Like me?</i>

271
00:22:49,410 --> 00:22:51,536
Grandpa...

272
00:23:36,124 --> 00:23:40,425
I went to the funeral hall,
but they said you went home.

273
00:23:43,382 --> 00:23:45,159
Are you okay?

274
00:23:46,457 --> 00:23:47,635
And if not...

275
00:23:47,635 --> 00:23:50,122
- What should I do?
- Hug me.

276
00:24:10,107 --> 00:24:13,065
I don't know any better way to comfort you.

277
00:24:13,065 --> 00:24:17,391
But I felt like Grandpa would be in here.

278
00:25:26,775 --> 00:25:28,313
What the hell?

279
00:25:30,899 --> 00:25:32,387
Listen to me.

280
00:25:32,387 --> 00:25:36,339
Watch your language. Okay?

281
00:25:38,288 --> 00:25:41,325
This bastard is so funny.

282
00:25:42,125 --> 00:25:45,461
Why's he acting like he's the victim?

283
00:25:45,461 --> 00:25:46,486
Why?

284
00:25:46,486 --> 00:25:49,246
It's my fault, all my fault. Happy?

285
00:25:57,850 --> 00:26:00,260
Seriously, I said I'm not eating.

286
00:26:04,858 --> 00:26:06,108
Hey.

287
00:26:06,108 --> 00:26:11,887
After my tractor accident,
that woman did something to me.

288
00:26:11,887 --> 00:26:13,126
Do you know what it was?

289
00:26:14,399 --> 00:26:15,742
Don't say it!

290
00:26:15,742 --> 00:26:17,694
Stop it. Stop it.

291
00:26:17,694 --> 00:26:19,443
Really...

292
00:26:21,830 --> 00:26:27,795
I was in the hospital, fighting for my life.

293
00:26:27,795 --> 00:26:32,763
But she went home to sleep every night
because you kept crying for Mom.

294
00:26:32,763 --> 00:26:34,314
You brat.

295
00:26:34,998 --> 00:26:36,680
So what?

296
00:26:36,680 --> 00:26:39,719
You're not the only one who needed a mom!

297
00:26:40,721 --> 00:26:44,043
I needed her too!

298
00:26:44,043 --> 00:26:46,107
Mom! Mom!

299
00:26:46,107 --> 00:26:49,370
I was, what, one or two!

300
00:26:50,527 --> 00:26:53,316
I was six!

301
00:26:54,625 --> 00:26:55,999
Only six!

302
00:26:58,116 --> 00:27:01,694
You think only you were little?

303
00:27:02,387 --> 00:27:05,482
I was little too!

304
00:27:05,482 --> 00:27:11,421
I was scared as hell, and Mom wasn't there.

305
00:27:11,421 --> 00:27:16,345
I suddenly couldn't hear or speak!

306
00:27:16,345 --> 00:27:18,804
But she wasn't there! Why?

307
00:27:18,804 --> 00:27:21,098
Because of you!

308
00:27:21,098 --> 00:27:24,610
You're not the only one who lost a mom!

309
00:27:33,443 --> 00:27:35,429
- Jeez!
- Stop it.

310
00:27:35,429 --> 00:27:38,640
Get out. You too. Both of you, get out!

311
00:27:38,640 --> 00:27:40,174
Mom.

312
00:27:40,869 --> 00:27:42,262
Enough, all of you.

313
00:27:42,262 --> 00:27:45,065
It's been ages since we were all together.

314
00:27:45,065 --> 00:27:46,597
Grandpa...

315
00:27:48,232 --> 00:27:52,723
If Father saw this, he would be speechless.

316
00:27:54,216 --> 00:27:56,399
It's bad enough.

317
00:27:56,399 --> 00:27:59,190
No one came to save him.

318
00:27:59,190 --> 00:28:01,078
And he was alone in there...

319
00:28:01,078 --> 00:28:02,482
<i>Hello, sir.</i>

320
00:28:02,482 --> 00:28:04,226
<i>- Hello.
- Hello, sir.</i>

321
00:28:04,226 --> 00:28:06,281
<i>- Hello.
- Hello.</i>

322
00:28:12,582 --> 00:28:14,652
<i>Jae Jin.</i>

323
00:28:14,652 --> 00:28:16,936
<i>Were you happy?</i>

324
00:28:20,200 --> 00:28:23,284
<i>I was happy. I'm sure of it.</i>

325
00:28:25,423 --> 00:28:28,642
<i>Was I the only one who was happy
when I made all of that?</i>

326
00:28:30,208 --> 00:28:34,221
<i>The people who made it, my family...</i>

327
00:28:34,221 --> 00:28:36,650
<i>And everyone else here...</i>

328
00:28:36,650 --> 00:28:39,447
<i>I believe they were all happy.</i>

329
00:28:39,447 --> 00:28:44,388
<i>I believed I had to make this to be happy.</i>

330
00:28:45,315 --> 00:28:46,980
<i>That's why...</i>

331
00:28:48,884 --> 00:28:52,201
<i>I never let you do anything you wanted.</i>

332
00:28:54,537 --> 00:28:55,877
<i>Father.</i>

333
00:28:57,277 --> 00:29:00,649
<i>Father, I don't blame you.</i>

334
00:29:00,649 --> 00:29:01,753
<i>I just...</i>

335
00:29:01,753 --> 00:29:03,137
<i>All right.</i>

336
00:29:03,137 --> 00:29:07,528
<i>You traded your happiness for this.</i>

337
00:29:11,576 --> 00:29:13,851
<i>Don't be bitter.</i>

338
00:29:14,670 --> 00:29:17,004
<i>You saved this place.</i>

339
00:29:18,151 --> 00:29:20,858
<i>Thank you for saving it.</i>

340
00:29:38,678 --> 00:29:40,614
But, I...

341
00:29:40,614 --> 00:29:42,988
I couldn't even save Father...

342
00:29:53,296 --> 00:29:56,190
[Upo High School]

343
00:29:56,190 --> 00:29:58,149
- Hey!
- That hurts!

344
00:29:58,149 --> 00:29:59,688
Hey, Sung Sae Ryeong.

345
00:30:01,937 --> 00:30:03,649
Did you think about it?

346
00:30:03,649 --> 00:30:05,320
About me. Really deeply.

347
00:30:05,320 --> 00:30:06,387
No.

348
00:30:06,387 --> 00:30:08,190
Okay.

349
00:30:08,190 --> 00:30:11,190
So you heard I'm in the final, right?

350
00:30:11,190 --> 00:30:12,844
No.

351
00:30:12,844 --> 00:30:14,565
I made it to the final.

352
00:30:14,565 --> 00:30:15,993
You're coming, right?

353
00:30:15,993 --> 00:30:17,440
No.

354
00:30:17,440 --> 00:30:19,097
So did you break up with Cho Yu Gyeom?

355
00:30:19,097 --> 00:30:20,774
No.

356
00:30:20,774 --> 00:30:22,816
But he seems to be seeing someone else.

357
00:30:22,816 --> 00:30:24,190
No, it's not like that.

358
00:30:24,190 --> 00:30:25,482
What? I saw them.

359
00:30:25,482 --> 00:30:31,420
Holding hands with that girl, feeding her,
all lovey-dovey on the train.

360
00:30:31,420 --> 00:30:33,111
Hey, I'm seriously...

361
00:30:33,111 --> 00:30:34,274
It makes me cringe.

362
00:30:34,274 --> 00:30:36,755
She said she would break up with him.

363
00:30:36,755 --> 00:30:39,126
When vacation ends.

364
00:30:39,126 --> 00:30:41,010
<i>When summer ends.</i>

365
00:30:44,275 --> 00:30:46,838
<i>When the cicadas stop singing...</i>

366
00:30:48,070 --> 00:30:49,366
<i>We...</i>

367
00:30:50,123 --> 00:30:51,651
They will break up.

368
00:30:55,954 --> 00:30:59,337
I'm really going to take first place.
I'm going to be a big deal.

369
00:32:01,940 --> 00:32:04,010
Yes, what?

370
00:32:09,232 --> 00:32:11,217
Put Yu Gyeom on.

371
00:32:12,107 --> 00:32:13,380
Now.

372
00:32:33,940 --> 00:32:35,274
Okay.

373
00:32:35,274 --> 00:32:36,756
<i>Yu Gyeom.</i>

374
00:32:37,399 --> 00:32:39,364
Go ahead, Aunt.

375
00:32:46,304 --> 00:32:50,720
Do you want to live with me?

376
00:32:51,431 --> 00:32:55,816
Your dad told me not to come
to your house anymore.

377
00:32:55,816 --> 00:32:57,855
It makes your mom uncomfortable.

378
00:32:58,935 --> 00:33:00,321
<i>Then...</i>

379
00:33:01,065 --> 00:33:03,658
Will you see me on your own?

380
00:33:05,471 --> 00:33:07,559
You hate me.

381
00:33:09,691 --> 00:33:11,349
But Yu Gyeom...

382
00:33:15,796 --> 00:33:17,397
I...

383
00:33:19,247 --> 00:33:23,815
I really miss you.

384
00:33:23,815 --> 00:33:28,392
Because you're all I have.

385
00:33:32,431 --> 00:33:33,936
Even if...

386
00:33:35,482 --> 00:33:38,042
I'll put up with it if you call me Aunt.

387
00:33:39,009 --> 00:33:41,524
I know you're a little embarrassed by me...

388
00:33:41,524 --> 00:33:43,437
<i>Mom, you don't embarrass me.</i>

389
00:33:46,691 --> 00:33:48,100
I just...

390
00:33:50,162 --> 00:33:52,020
didn't like you.

391
00:33:54,076 --> 00:33:55,821
<i>I didn't like you.</i>

392
00:33:56,881 --> 00:33:59,042
<i>But I wasn't embarrassed.</i>

393
00:34:04,879 --> 00:34:07,202
It's just that someone I didn't like...

394
00:34:09,107 --> 00:34:14,162
turning out to be my real mom
made it even worse.

395
00:34:17,315 --> 00:34:19,560
But now I don't dislike you.

396
00:34:19,560 --> 00:34:21,597
Not that I like you, either.

397
00:34:26,231 --> 00:34:27,675
Still...

398
00:34:29,982 --> 00:34:32,096
I just want to live here.

399
00:34:34,307 --> 00:34:36,329
If you want to see me,

400
00:34:38,065 --> 00:34:40,405
call Dad, and we'll meet up.

401
00:34:41,954 --> 00:34:47,034
We can have a meal and watch a movie.

402
00:34:52,173 --> 00:34:56,513
When fall comes, we can go to the mountains.

403
00:35:01,982 --> 00:35:04,401
Thank you for running to me.

404
00:35:07,816 --> 00:35:09,448
For having me...

405
00:35:12,362 --> 00:35:14,102
For giving birth to me,

406
00:35:15,691 --> 00:35:17,411
thank you for that too.

407
00:35:29,880 --> 00:35:31,331
But...

408
00:35:34,698 --> 00:35:36,781
The person who raised me,

409
00:35:38,399 --> 00:35:40,101
that's who I'll live with.

410
00:36:00,134 --> 00:36:01,380
Hey.

411
00:36:04,443 --> 00:36:05,823
Bye.

412
00:36:08,896 --> 00:36:10,103
Okay.

413
00:36:11,505 --> 00:36:14,662
I heard you made Sung Sae Ryeong do it.

414
00:36:14,662 --> 00:36:15,998
To apologize.

415
00:36:17,971 --> 00:36:19,269
Yes.

416
00:36:19,269 --> 00:36:20,747
Why did you do that?

417
00:36:22,607 --> 00:36:25,034
Because you apologized to me too.

418
00:36:38,407 --> 00:36:40,448
- Did she swear at you?
- Stop it.

419
00:36:40,448 --> 00:36:42,179
Really.

420
00:36:44,913 --> 00:36:46,745
I'll go first.

421
00:37:22,332 --> 00:37:24,438
Mom, I'm heading out.

422
00:37:24,438 --> 00:37:26,799
Okay, go.

423
00:37:37,566 --> 00:37:39,190
Why?

424
00:37:39,190 --> 00:37:40,390
What?

425
00:37:41,149 --> 00:37:42,982
I'm not asking you to.

426
00:37:42,982 --> 00:37:46,060
I'll do it all myself.

427
00:37:48,318 --> 00:37:49,813
Jung Yeon.

428
00:37:50,423 --> 00:37:51,980
Yes? What?

429
00:37:51,980 --> 00:37:53,767
You help Mom out.

430
00:37:57,194 --> 00:38:00,658
Oh my, what's gotten into her?

431
00:38:00,658 --> 00:38:02,649
Never mind.

432
00:38:02,649 --> 00:38:04,429
I can do it myself.

433
00:38:04,429 --> 00:38:05,835
Dad.

434
00:38:06,787 --> 00:38:08,421
What?

435
00:38:08,421 --> 00:38:09,596
What?

436
00:38:09,596 --> 00:38:11,418
You help out too, Dad.

437
00:38:14,322 --> 00:38:17,687
Dad, Jung Yeon, you help Mom pack too.

438
00:38:17,687 --> 00:38:20,055
From now on, pack your own stuff.

439
00:38:20,691 --> 00:38:24,777
Mom and Dad both work,
so why does Mom do all the housework?

440
00:38:24,777 --> 00:38:26,399
Dad, you do it too.

441
00:38:26,399 --> 00:38:28,054
Jung Yeon too.

442
00:38:29,965 --> 00:38:33,691
What's gotten into her?

443
00:38:33,691 --> 00:38:35,357
Just go.

444
00:38:35,357 --> 00:38:39,651
Go out for your nightly walk like a dog.

445
00:38:39,651 --> 00:38:43,862
Go have fun with that wonderful
boyfriend of yours.

446
00:38:43,862 --> 00:38:45,479
Okay.

447
00:38:45,479 --> 00:38:47,017
I'll have fun.

448
00:38:47,017 --> 00:38:49,598
When I'm back, I'll pack my own stuff.

449
00:38:50,484 --> 00:38:53,718
Honestly, is that her being a good daughter?

450
00:38:53,718 --> 00:38:55,669
I'll be late.

451
00:38:55,669 --> 00:38:57,111
Why, that...

452
00:38:57,111 --> 00:38:58,719
What's she saying?

453
00:38:58,719 --> 00:39:04,428
Did she just sweet-talk me into accepting
that she'll be late?

454
00:39:04,428 --> 00:39:06,388
Seriously.

455
00:39:06,388 --> 00:39:08,094
- Honestly.
- Mom.

456
00:39:08,954 --> 00:39:11,464
I'll pack my things and come out.

457
00:39:27,510 --> 00:39:29,416
And you? What are you doing?

458
00:39:30,384 --> 00:39:32,084
You pack too.

459
00:39:32,084 --> 00:39:34,018
Didn't you hear Ha Yeon?

460
00:39:48,168 --> 00:39:49,578
Are you cold?

461
00:39:50,258 --> 00:39:51,994
No.

462
00:39:55,852 --> 00:39:57,524
It's so cold.

463
00:39:57,524 --> 00:40:02,905
<i>That night was the last night
we spent together.</i>

464
00:40:12,082 --> 00:40:13,882
This is the song from before.

465
00:40:13,882 --> 00:40:15,120
Right?

466
00:40:19,604 --> 00:40:21,312
When do you leave tomorrow?

467
00:40:23,894 --> 00:40:25,269
Afternoon?

468
00:40:26,357 --> 00:40:27,858
Let's meet before you go.

469
00:40:27,858 --> 00:40:29,787
I have something for you.

470
00:40:30,428 --> 00:40:31,721
Okay.

471
00:40:31,721 --> 00:40:34,449
I have something for you too.

472
00:40:34,449 --> 00:40:35,596
Really?

473
00:40:35,596 --> 00:40:36,822
Yes.

474
00:40:38,443 --> 00:40:39,719
What could it be?

475
00:40:40,334 --> 00:40:42,544
What could it be?

476
00:40:43,358 --> 00:40:45,320
- Can't wait.
- No.

477
00:40:45,320 --> 00:40:47,607
- Don't get your hopes up.
- They're already way up.

478
00:40:47,607 --> 00:40:53,561
<i>We gave it our all during that time
and promised never to forget that day.</i>

479
00:41:01,376 --> 00:41:04,207
- It's all ready.
- It looks delicious.

480
00:41:04,207 --> 00:41:06,339
Sam Hee.

481
00:41:06,339 --> 00:41:08,810
Everything's ready, so tell Grandpa...

482
00:41:09,940 --> 00:41:11,370
No, never mind.

483
00:41:12,182 --> 00:41:15,858
Tell your dad that it's time to eat.

484
00:41:15,858 --> 00:41:17,301
Yes, Mom.

485
00:41:18,887 --> 00:41:20,707
Sam Hee.

486
00:41:20,707 --> 00:41:22,646
Wake Dul Hee up too.

487
00:41:22,646 --> 00:41:24,097
Yes, Mom.

488
00:41:38,537 --> 00:41:41,395
<i>Did the funeral go well?</i>

489
00:41:47,899 --> 00:41:51,906
[It went well.]

490
00:42:06,482 --> 00:42:08,935
What? What are you doing?

491
00:42:11,065 --> 00:42:13,971
[I really can't make up with them.]

492
00:42:13,971 --> 00:42:19,265
[Can't I just apologize to Sam Hee and go?]

493
00:42:19,265 --> 00:42:23,752
<i>No, you can't.
And definitely not just with the little one.</i>

494
00:42:23,752 --> 00:42:26,711
<i>Send a photo with your parents and Yu Gyeom.</i>

495
00:42:26,711 --> 00:42:31,549
[Oppa, oppa, I love...]

496
00:42:31,549 --> 00:42:32,554
Mom.

497
00:42:32,554 --> 00:42:33,566
Yes?

498
00:42:33,566 --> 00:42:35,357
She's texting at the table.

499
00:42:35,357 --> 00:42:38,171
And she's telling some guy she loves him.

500
00:42:39,268 --> 00:42:42,698
Dul Hee, stop it. Eat.

501
00:42:45,137 --> 00:42:48,026
Dad, kick her out.
She's on her phone while eating.

502
00:42:48,026 --> 00:42:50,300
Grandpa would have killed her.

503
00:42:53,654 --> 00:42:55,357
Why did you hit me?

504
00:42:55,357 --> 00:42:57,992
Dul Hee, your little brother...

505
00:42:57,992 --> 00:43:00,554
Why are you hitting him? It's your fault.

506
00:43:00,554 --> 00:43:01,623
Right.

507
00:43:01,623 --> 00:43:04,960
Excuse me, lady.
Are you taking Cho Yu Gyeom's side again?

508
00:43:04,960 --> 00:43:06,982
Take your own kid's side!

509
00:43:06,982 --> 00:43:09,940
How can you call your mom "lady"?

510
00:43:09,940 --> 00:43:13,732
And you shouldn't tell guys
you love them so easily.

511
00:43:13,732 --> 00:43:15,280
Right, Sam Hee?

512
00:43:16,886 --> 00:43:18,858
Excuse me.

513
00:43:18,858 --> 00:43:20,765
Who are you, mister?

514
00:43:20,765 --> 00:43:23,994
Me? I'm your dad. Your father.

515
00:43:25,606 --> 00:43:27,149
You...

516
00:43:27,149 --> 00:43:28,984
You know sign language?

517
00:43:28,984 --> 00:43:32,029
It's been years. Of course I picked it up.

518
00:43:32,029 --> 00:43:36,716
Hey, so you're showing off
because she's your mom?

519
00:43:39,870 --> 00:43:43,453
Of course she's my mom. Is she yours?

520
00:43:45,348 --> 00:43:46,958
Yu Gyeom.

521
00:43:46,958 --> 00:43:48,334
- Not yet.
- It's too good to waste.

522
00:43:48,334 --> 00:43:51,507
Who knew a birth secret
would end up as a joke like this?

523
00:43:51,507 --> 00:43:53,591
Grandpa never saw this coming.

524
00:43:54,882 --> 00:43:55,925
<i>Got a minute?</i>

525
00:43:55,925 --> 00:43:57,094
Don't eat.

526
00:43:59,178 --> 00:44:00,807
Get out.

527
00:44:01,740 --> 00:44:03,359
- Thanks for the meal.
- Hey...

528
00:44:03,359 --> 00:44:05,646
Thank you for the meal. Mom, I'll be back.

529
00:44:05,646 --> 00:44:07,812
Go out together.

530
00:44:10,439 --> 00:44:12,168
Seriously, you...

531
00:44:12,168 --> 00:44:14,440
Great. Just great.

532
00:44:14,440 --> 00:44:16,211
It went inside.

533
00:44:19,481 --> 00:44:24,922
By the way, why does your second
sister hit your little brother so much?

534
00:44:25,830 --> 00:44:31,357
Her own mom only adored Yu Gyeom,
so she beat him up every time she saw him.

535
00:44:31,357 --> 00:44:33,483
My sister has a nasty temper.

536
00:44:34,255 --> 00:44:36,120
That's a very primal reason.

537
00:44:36,120 --> 00:44:38,811
Kids are all primal.

538
00:44:38,811 --> 00:44:41,164
But she's still like that as an adult.

539
00:44:41,164 --> 00:44:44,289
My sister's still just as primal.

540
00:44:49,023 --> 00:44:50,598
When are you leaving?

541
00:44:50,598 --> 00:44:52,185
In a bit.

542
00:44:56,530 --> 00:44:58,370
Have a safe trip.

543
00:44:58,370 --> 00:45:00,301
Stay healthy.

544
00:45:01,156 --> 00:45:03,284
And...

545
00:45:03,284 --> 00:45:07,955
Get a better score
in sign language class next time.

546
00:45:07,955 --> 00:45:09,539
Or did you already do well?

547
00:45:09,539 --> 00:45:11,190
I don't know.

548
00:45:11,190 --> 00:45:12,634
And...

549
00:45:13,461 --> 00:45:18,687
I hope you won't feel guilty anymore.

550
00:45:18,687 --> 00:45:20,119
And...

551
00:45:25,561 --> 00:45:27,411
That really sounds like goodbye.

552
00:45:27,411 --> 00:45:29,487
It is a goodbye.

553
00:45:31,275 --> 00:45:33,085
Have a safe trip.

554
00:45:34,023 --> 00:45:36,279
We had fun, didn't we?

555
00:45:37,538 --> 00:45:39,313
It's not goodbye for me.

556
00:45:39,940 --> 00:45:41,346
What?

557
00:45:41,346 --> 00:45:43,726
I'm going to keep seeing you, Sam Hee.

558
00:45:46,899 --> 00:45:48,083
But...

559
00:45:50,014 --> 00:45:53,167
How can a Seoul guy and an Upo-ri girl...

560
00:45:53,167 --> 00:45:57,473
I mean, it's so far away.

561
00:45:57,473 --> 00:46:00,215
It takes two hours from here to Seoul.

562
00:46:00,215 --> 00:46:02,270
It's only two hours.

563
00:46:02,270 --> 00:46:05,981
Crossing Seoul in a traffic jam
can take more than two hours.

564
00:46:06,725 --> 00:46:09,229
From here, it's two hours on one train.

565
00:46:10,351 --> 00:46:12,606
- But...
- And this.

566
00:46:13,615 --> 00:46:15,482
What is this?

567
00:46:15,482 --> 00:46:18,969
You said you want to study and go to college.

568
00:46:18,969 --> 00:46:20,801
Then that textbook will help.

569
00:46:20,801 --> 00:46:24,865
To retake the exam, you'll need to go
to a cram school in Seoul anyway.

570
00:46:24,865 --> 00:46:27,089
I don't see how this is goodbye.

571
00:46:29,831 --> 00:46:32,961
But you have friends in Seoul, Jung Yeon.

572
00:46:32,961 --> 00:46:34,952
But my girlfriend is here.

573
00:46:41,343 --> 00:46:43,321
Come on, keep walking.

574
00:46:53,843 --> 00:46:55,892
The weather's great.

575
00:46:57,553 --> 00:47:00,400
So this feels good when you do it.

576
00:47:00,400 --> 00:47:01,677
Right?

577
00:47:01,677 --> 00:47:02,858
Yes.

578
00:47:02,858 --> 00:47:04,874
I feel so good.

579
00:47:41,149 --> 00:47:42,429
What's this?

580
00:47:42,429 --> 00:47:43,566
This?

581
00:47:43,566 --> 00:47:45,044
A mixtape.

582
00:47:46,029 --> 00:47:48,346
- A mixtape?
- Yes.

583
00:47:48,346 --> 00:47:51,537
You know the songs we listened to at the cabin?

584
00:47:51,537 --> 00:47:54,000
I recorded them all on it.

585
00:47:59,922 --> 00:48:01,350
Thank you.

586
00:48:02,107 --> 00:48:04,149
You have a Walkman or something?

587
00:48:04,774 --> 00:48:06,201
A Walkman?

588
00:48:08,889 --> 00:48:10,316
Here.

589
00:48:10,316 --> 00:48:12,018
You can listen with this.

590
00:48:16,401 --> 00:48:18,478
It looks like an antique.

591
00:48:19,105 --> 00:48:21,607
It is an antique. It's my dad's.

592
00:48:21,607 --> 00:48:22,679
What?

593
00:48:23,473 --> 00:48:26,873
Is it okay if I take your dad's stuff?

594
00:48:26,873 --> 00:48:28,406
I stole it.

595
00:48:29,251 --> 00:48:30,737
Is that okay?

596
00:48:30,737 --> 00:48:32,264
It's fine.

597
00:48:32,264 --> 00:48:35,397
He'll probably never look for it.

598
00:48:41,090 --> 00:48:42,627
This is for you.

599
00:48:43,574 --> 00:48:44,935
What is this?

600
00:48:46,573 --> 00:48:50,277
I took notes for the classes you missed.

601
00:48:50,277 --> 00:48:52,558
I'm good at taking notes.

602
00:48:52,558 --> 00:48:53,933
Seems like it.

603
00:49:06,554 --> 00:49:08,617
I'll treasure it.

604
00:49:10,620 --> 00:49:13,555
Yes, please treasure it.

605
00:49:17,624 --> 00:49:19,384
But, Yu Gyeom...

606
00:49:20,449 --> 00:49:21,571
Yes.

607
00:49:26,858 --> 00:49:30,833
Are we breaking up now?

608
00:49:39,190 --> 00:49:40,326
Yes.

609
00:49:43,042 --> 00:49:44,194
Why?

610
00:49:47,107 --> 00:49:49,282
<i>Yu Gyeom answered.</i>

611
00:49:51,350 --> 00:49:55,564
<i>Because vacation is over.</i>

612
00:50:06,340 --> 00:50:07,795
Wait.

613
00:50:36,828 --> 00:50:40,575
<i>You smelled like summer.</i>

614
00:50:41,992 --> 00:50:44,141
<i>Hey, give me back my ice cream.</i>

615
00:50:44,141 --> 00:50:46,315
<i>- Do you want to?
- Give me my ice cream!</i>

616
00:50:46,315 --> 00:50:48,137
<i>- This.
- My ice cream!</i>

617
00:50:48,137 --> 00:50:49,607
<i>Thank you.</i>

618
00:50:49,607 --> 00:50:51,770
<i>- Come catch me.
- I'll go and do well.</i>

619
00:50:56,149 --> 00:50:59,193
<i>Final exams were over.</i>

620
00:50:59,193 --> 00:51:02,479
<i>The walk home was sweet.</i>

621
00:51:02,479 --> 00:51:06,184
<i>It was sticky like soda,
with the raw smell of green grass.</i>

622
00:51:14,420 --> 00:51:17,000
<i>Summer exists in this world.</i>

623
00:51:17,000 --> 00:51:20,971
<i>Summer returns every year without fail.</i>

624
00:51:20,971 --> 00:51:24,333
<i>I'll remember you.</i>

625
00:51:46,232 --> 00:51:50,631
She always gets the last nice word in.

626
00:51:56,043 --> 00:51:58,043
<i>Sung Sae Ryeong.</i>

627
00:51:58,043 --> 00:52:02,459
<i>I think you can become a good adult in the end.</i>

628
00:52:02,459 --> 00:52:07,114
<i>Because we got a little better.</i>

629
00:52:37,791 --> 00:52:39,607
Hey, what are you doing?

630
00:52:39,607 --> 00:52:41,107
Get in, hurry!

631
00:52:58,423 --> 00:53:02,304
<i>Some music reminds you of rain.</i>

632
00:53:02,304 --> 00:53:05,437
<i>Other music reminds you of summer.</i>

633
00:53:06,982 --> 00:53:11,281
<i>You were that music for me.</i>

634
00:53:13,900 --> 00:53:18,714
<i>Whenever I play it,
the world I shared with you unfolds.</i>

635
00:53:20,691 --> 00:53:25,647
<i>You have no idea how much that will comfort me.</i>

636
00:53:35,940 --> 00:53:40,399
<i>The 22nd national swimming championships
were held today.</i>

637
00:53:40,399 --> 00:53:43,816
<i>Cho Yu Gyeom of Upo High School
was a favorite to win.</i>

638
00:53:43,816 --> 00:53:47,566
<i>He finished third with a time of 1:49.91.</i>

639
00:53:47,566 --> 00:53:50,583
<i>Baek Seung Woo of Seondong High took second.</i>

640
00:53:50,583 --> 00:53:55,710
<i>As expected, Upo High School's Im Jeong Uk
won with a time of 1:49.08.</i>

641
00:53:57,042 --> 00:53:58,918
Yes, understood.

642
00:54:00,362 --> 00:54:01,445
Hey, Ho Jae.

643
00:54:01,445 --> 00:54:02,460
Yes, what is it?

644
00:54:02,460 --> 00:54:05,691
After homeroom, tell Kim Ha Yeon B to see me.

645
00:54:05,691 --> 00:54:06,870
Okay.

646
00:54:08,599 --> 00:54:10,763
Im Jeong Uk.

647
00:54:10,763 --> 00:54:17,274
Winner of the 22nd
national swimming championships!

648
00:54:17,274 --> 00:54:18,579
Give him a hand!

649
00:54:24,190 --> 00:54:27,023
But you don't need to wear the medal here.

650
00:54:27,023 --> 00:54:28,816
What are you talking about?

651
00:54:28,816 --> 00:54:30,729
I have been wearing it for days.

652
00:54:30,729 --> 00:54:32,648
Suit yourself.

653
00:54:32,648 --> 00:54:33,812
Of course.

654
00:54:33,812 --> 00:54:39,979
Im Jeong Uk's win came after favorite Cho
Yu Gyeom slumped due to skipped training.

655
00:54:39,979 --> 00:54:41,346
And...

656
00:54:41,346 --> 00:54:44,149
Favorite Baek Seung Woo also
suffered a minor injury.

657
00:54:44,149 --> 00:54:45,649
Come on!

658
00:54:45,649 --> 00:54:48,315
It might look like a fluke.

659
00:54:48,315 --> 00:54:52,460
But during that short competition,
our Im Jeong Uk improved his time.

660
00:54:52,460 --> 00:54:54,793
He shaved a whole two seconds off it!

661
00:54:58,357 --> 00:55:00,858
Sometimes Salieri beats Beethoven.

662
00:55:00,858 --> 00:55:02,149
Come on!

663
00:55:02,149 --> 00:55:04,357
You could be Beethoven. Right, Cho Yu Gyeom?

664
00:55:04,357 --> 00:55:05,691
No, I'm Beethoven.

665
00:55:05,691 --> 00:55:09,216
Yes, obviously. It's me, right?

666
00:55:09,216 --> 00:55:10,720
Enough.

667
00:55:13,602 --> 00:55:16,399
But why am I always the last to know?

668
00:55:16,399 --> 00:55:18,148
All right, enough.

669
00:55:18,148 --> 00:55:24,115
The most important thing is that our school
has such outstanding people.

670
00:55:24,115 --> 00:55:27,149
So be a little proud, okay?

671
00:55:27,149 --> 00:55:28,566
Next, someone else steps up.

672
00:55:28,566 --> 00:55:31,208
Let's go out there and win again.

673
00:55:31,208 --> 00:55:32,216
Okay?

674
00:55:32,216 --> 00:55:33,691
- Okay!
- Okay!

675
00:55:33,691 --> 00:55:35,294
Free time. Jump in!

676
00:55:35,294 --> 00:55:37,294
- Jump in!
- Jump in!

677
00:55:41,982 --> 00:55:43,137
Hey.

678
00:55:43,137 --> 00:55:45,150
I asked out Sung Sae Ryeong.

679
00:55:48,691 --> 00:55:50,046
I got turned down.

680
00:55:52,149 --> 00:55:54,680
<i>Yes. I'll pass.</i>

681
00:55:56,732 --> 00:55:57,774
<i>Why not?</i>

682
00:55:57,774 --> 00:55:59,127
<i>But I came in first.</i>

683
00:55:59,127 --> 00:56:00,659
<i>I even beat Cho Yu Gyeom.</i>

684
00:56:00,659 --> 00:56:03,107
<i>I still like Cho Yu Gyeom.</i>

685
00:56:03,107 --> 00:56:04,429
<i>What?</i>

686
00:56:04,429 --> 00:56:05,814
<i>Are you two back together?</i>

687
00:56:05,814 --> 00:56:08,160
<i>No, I like Cho Yu Gyeom.</i>

688
00:56:08,160 --> 00:56:09,676
<i>That can happen.</i>

689
00:56:11,455 --> 00:56:12,776
<i>No.</i>

690
00:56:13,982 --> 00:56:15,624
<i>Congrats on coming in first.</i>

691
00:56:15,624 --> 00:56:20,672
<i>Congrats. But your win will always be framed
around the two people I mentioned...</i>

692
00:56:20,672 --> 00:56:21,963
<i>Knock it off.</i>

693
00:56:28,440 --> 00:56:33,296
Hey, speaking of which,
are you getting back with Sung Sae Ryeong?

694
00:56:33,296 --> 00:56:37,064
Will you tell me if you get back together
or if you break up?

695
00:56:37,064 --> 00:56:39,526
If you guys break up, I'll be right there...

696
00:56:39,526 --> 00:56:41,440
Jeong Uk.

697
00:56:41,440 --> 00:56:43,153
Someday...

698
00:56:43,153 --> 00:56:47,958
You'll be grateful that
Sung Sae Ryeong dumped you.

699
00:56:47,958 --> 00:56:49,930
- What?
- I'm going.

700
00:56:49,930 --> 00:56:52,412
Don't talk to me anymore. We're not friends.

701
00:56:52,412 --> 00:56:53,634
What?

702
00:56:57,739 --> 00:57:01,107
Hello. I'm here from Upo High School.

703
00:57:01,107 --> 00:57:03,274
So you came in third, not first?

704
00:57:03,274 --> 00:57:05,170
How do you feel?

705
00:57:09,023 --> 00:57:10,899
Hey. Didn't you see him the other day?

706
00:57:10,899 --> 00:57:13,138
I'm going to practice.

707
00:57:13,138 --> 00:57:15,179
- Again?
- What did you practice?

708
00:57:15,179 --> 00:57:17,224
What could it be?

709
00:57:35,950 --> 00:57:41,012
Did that nerve of yours that ran away
ever come back?

710
00:57:43,858 --> 00:57:47,001
No, it didn't.

711
00:57:48,281 --> 00:57:49,623
What?

712
00:57:53,563 --> 00:57:56,283
So stop talking to me.

713
00:57:58,923 --> 00:58:00,381
You...

714
00:58:03,984 --> 00:58:05,961
If you apologize to me now...

715
00:58:05,961 --> 00:58:08,697
I'm not apologizing to you.

716
00:58:08,697 --> 00:58:12,062
Because you're the one who owes me an apology.

717
00:58:12,743 --> 00:58:14,315
Hey, Kim Ha Yeon.

718
00:58:14,315 --> 00:58:15,794
Kim Ha Yeon!

719
00:58:17,073 --> 00:58:19,133
Hey, our teacher wants you in the office.

720
00:58:19,133 --> 00:58:20,315
Me?

721
00:58:20,315 --> 00:58:21,357
Really? Me?

722
00:58:21,357 --> 00:58:22,791
Yes, you're Kim Ha Yeon B.

723
00:58:22,791 --> 00:58:25,079
Seriously, I told you I'm not.

724
00:58:25,079 --> 00:58:26,089
I'm Kim Ha Yeon...

725
00:58:26,089 --> 00:58:27,503
Excuse me...

726
00:58:30,171 --> 00:58:32,188
I'm Kim Ha Yeon B.

727
00:58:33,067 --> 00:58:34,274
Really?

728
00:58:34,274 --> 00:58:36,473
You got it wrong last time too.

729
00:58:37,198 --> 00:58:39,156
She's A.

730
00:58:39,156 --> 00:58:40,605
I'm B.

731
00:58:41,730 --> 00:58:44,332
Okay, got it. Sorry.

732
00:58:44,332 --> 00:58:46,232
Then remember it.

733
00:58:46,232 --> 00:58:49,188
Don't just call anyone B if you don't know.

734
00:58:50,482 --> 00:58:53,149
Could you hold this broom for a sec?

735
00:58:54,304 --> 00:58:55,667
Thanks.

736
01:00:22,607 --> 01:00:26,722
<i>That summer, we definitely grew up.</i>

737
01:00:47,535 --> 01:00:52,243
Kim Ha Yeon B, you took supplementary classes
in the countryside?

738
01:00:52,243 --> 01:00:53,399
Yes.

739
01:00:53,399 --> 01:00:56,699
Is your goal still a mid-tier
four-year university in Seoul?

740
01:00:56,699 --> 01:00:59,332
And your major depends on your scores?

741
01:01:03,816 --> 01:01:05,266
Has that changed?

742
01:01:05,266 --> 01:01:07,744
Yes, it has.

743
01:01:07,744 --> 01:01:09,503
How?

744
01:01:09,503 --> 01:01:11,358
I chose a major.

745
01:01:12,489 --> 01:01:13,805
Right?

746
01:01:14,982 --> 01:01:18,133
Which major will it be?

747
01:01:18,133 --> 01:01:23,357
Korean Language and Literature,
because I like reading and writing.

748
01:01:23,357 --> 01:01:24,441
Really?

749
01:01:25,340 --> 01:01:27,604
Let's see.

750
01:01:27,604 --> 01:01:30,330
And I like watching movies too.

751
01:01:31,178 --> 01:01:32,857
What movies do you like?

752
01:01:33,939 --> 01:01:35,627
"Clueless"?

753
01:01:36,633 --> 01:01:37,971
What's that?

754
01:01:40,409 --> 01:01:43,888
It's old, so I thought you would know.

755
01:01:43,888 --> 01:01:45,331
Hey.

756
01:01:46,149 --> 01:01:47,992
I'm young.

757
01:01:50,851 --> 01:01:53,283
I'm younger, though.

758
01:01:54,794 --> 01:01:56,387
Right.

759
01:01:56,387 --> 01:01:58,262
If it's movies...

760
01:01:59,344 --> 01:02:01,566
There's also a Visual Arts major.

761
01:02:01,566 --> 01:02:02,719
Right.

762
01:02:02,719 --> 01:02:08,315
And Theater and Film, and Media Studies...
they're all in that area, you know?

763
01:02:08,315 --> 01:02:10,691
I should have studied harder.

764
01:02:10,691 --> 01:02:12,884
Not enough points for Media Studies.

765
01:02:12,884 --> 01:02:18,736
<i>When another summer comes again,
when those hot days suddenly arrive...</i>

766
01:02:20,065 --> 01:02:24,186
<i>I, too, will think of you.</i>

767
01:02:47,691 --> 01:02:51,402
<i>Like the music we listened to on that tape,</i>

768
01:02:53,398 --> 01:02:56,888
<i>I'll fill myself with you and never forget.</i>

769
01:02:58,237 --> 01:02:59,708
<i>Cho Yu Gyeom.</i>

770
01:03:03,460 --> 01:03:04,680
<i>Yes.</i>

771
01:03:05,407 --> 01:03:07,635
<i>I won't forget you either.</i>

772
01:03:07,635 --> 01:03:08,964
<i>Kim Ha Yeon.</i>
